WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:14.730
X fourteen is the Second Isogonic Center of triangle A B C: erect equilateral triangles inward across sides B C, C A, and A B, join their apexes to the opposite vertices A, B, and C, and those three lines concur at X fourteen.

2
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:26.850
Its trilinear coordinates replace plus pi over three with minus pi over three: cosecant of A minus pi over three, to cosecant of B minus pi over three, to cosecant of C minus pi over three.

3
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:38.240
On the central lines layer, X fourteen joins X thirteen and the Symmedian point X six on line six, thirteen, fourteen, and joins X two and X fifteen, as well as X three and X eighteen.

4
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:52.380
Under functional relations, X fourteen is the isogonal conjugate of the Second Isodynamic Point X sixteen, the orthocentroidal-circle inverse of X thirteen, and the reflection of X thirteen across the Kiepert center X one hundred fifteen.
